          "citations": null,
          "text": "The number of representations r2(n) = 4(d1(n) − d3(n)). For n = 5^10, the only prime factor is 5, which is 1 mod 4, so r2 = 4(10+1) = 44.\n\nCheck with a small case: 5^1 = 5 has r2 = 4·2 = 8, namely (±1, ±2) and (±2, ±1), which is 8 pairs. This matches.\n\nSo for 5^10 the count is 44.\n\n{\"answer\": 44, \"note\": \"r2(5^10)=4*(10+1)=44\"}",
